Tried 3.10-rc4 on my testbed and 3 machines report problems with MTRR 
cleanup. Two of them were different P3 PCs both with i815 chipset, and 
third was dual P3 server with Gigabyte 6ETXDR mainboard (Broadcom 
CNB20LE chipset).

On one of them, with 3.10-rc3 I saw
[    0.000000] MTRR variable ranges enabled:
[    0.000000]   0 base 000000000 mask FE0000000 write-back
[    0.000000]   1 base 01FF00000 mask FFFF00000 uncachable
[    0.000000]   2 disabled
[    0.000000]   3 disabled
[    0.000000]   4 disabled
[    0.000000]   5 disabled
[    0.000000]   6 disabled
[    0.000000]   7 disabled
[    0.000000] PAT not supported by CPU.
[    0.000000] original variable MTRRs
[    0.000000] reg 0, base: 0GB, range: 512MB, type WB
[    0.000000] reg 1, base: 511MB, range: 1MB, type UC
[    0.000000] total RAM covered: 511M
[    0.000000] Found optimal setting for mtrr clean up
[    0.000000]  gran_size: 64K  chunk_size: 2M  num_reg: 2      lose cover RAM: 0G
[    0.000000] New variable MTRRs
[    0.000000] reg 0, base: 0GB, range: 512MB, type WB
[    0.000000] reg 1, base: 511MB, range: 1MB, type UC

and 3.10-rc4 gives
MTRR default type: uncachable
MTRR fixed ranges enabled:
  00000-9FFFF write-back
  A0000-BFFFF uncachable
  C0000-CFFFF write-protect
  D0000-DFFFF uncachable
